13	% io_loadspec_sdat outputs the data in structure format, with fields 
14	% corresponding to time scale, fids, frequency scale, spectra, and header 
15	% fields containing information about the acquisition.  The resulting 
16	% matlab structure can be operated on by the other functions in this MRS 
17	% toolbox. ALSO:  This code is not currently smart enough to parse out all 
18	% of the relevant information from the header file, such as the number of 
19	% subspectra.  So for now, these details must be passed to the function as 
20	% input arguments.  Help implementing these improvements are most welcome!!
21	% 
22	% INPUTS:
23	% filename   = filename of Philips sdat file to be loaded.
24	% subspecs   = number of subspectra in the data (from spectral editing, ISIS, etc.)
25	%
26	% OUTPUTS:
27	% out        = Input dataset in FID-A structure format.
